# AI Test Orchestrator — Cursor Rules

## Project Overview
Reusable AI-driven end-to-end testing framework. Three-agent architecture: Player Agent → SUT → Judge Agent. Framework-agnostic — application-specific invariants and adapters live in consuming repos.

## Architecture
- `SUTAdapter` protocol is THE integration point. Never add game/app-specific logic to the framework.
- `InvariantCheck` protocol: name, severity, check(turn_result, world_state, history) → CheckResult.
- `BaseInvariantCheck` provides `_pass()` and `_fail()` helpers. Subclass this for convenience.
- `TurnResult` is frozen (immutable). Never mutate it.
- `NarrativeJudge` is optional (behind `[llm]` extra). Must work in offline mode (zero scores).

## Code Style
- Python 3.11+. Use `from __future__ import annotations` everywhere.
- Ruff for linting and formatting (see pyproject.toml).
- All public functions and classes need docstrings.
- Type hints on all function signatures.
- Tests use pytest. Each module has a corresponding `test_*.py`.

## Key Rules
- NEVER add application-specific logic (no GURPS, no d20, no NPC, no combat references).
- The framework must work with ANY SUT that implements the protocol.
- All randomness must be seedable for deterministic replay.
- Severity levels: CRITICAL fails suite (fail-fast halts), ERROR fails test, WARNING logs only.
- Reports are JSON. Transcripts are JSONL. Both go in test_results/.
- Pre-commit hook runs ruff. Configure with: `git config core.hooksPath .githooks`
